      reading:[choice("What happens if a conservative bounding-box test lets through a segment that misses every pixel in the tile?",["The exact shader does an extra test and rejects it harmlessly","A real visible pixel disappears","The false segment overwrites the true winner"],0,"False positives only add narrow-phase work while preserving exact output; false negatives (a box that's too tight) corrupt the image.")],
      recall:[reasoning("What shared data do pixel threads in a tile reuse, and what two barrier ordering rules does that require?","They share each batch of surviving segments (geometry + original IDs). Barrier 1 ensures the whole batch is written before pixels read it; barrier 2 ensures all pixels finish reading before the next batch overwrites shared memory.")],
      "practice.0":[list("Against tile [0, 15] × [0, 15] using inclusive bounds, enter 1 (keep) or 0 (reject) for these three boxes in order: [17, 21]×[2, 8], [15, 17]×[2, 8], and [−2, −1]×[−4, 20].",[0,1,0],"Box 1 lies strictly right of 15 (reject); box 2 touches along x = 15 (keep); box 3 lies strictly left of 0 even though y overlaps (reject).")],
